Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 04:45:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1135/1157] fix(update-pause): a paused turn waits on the
 apply, never a drainer that cannot apply [daveey]

t_01a18b11cabcd2c2, example-laptop 2026-10-29: two capped pauses (pauses >= MAX_PAUSES) parked for the
drainer's whole 66-min life after their window expired at 20:36:15 and were continued only at 21:25,
once the checkout moved. drain_retry_pending now parks at most PARK_MAX_S (600 s) from paused_at, then
continues in place while the drainer still runs. A turn paused STUCK_WARN_S (900 s) logs a WARNING naming
the session and what it waits on. read_turn_marker exposes paused_at.
